-2.  If true, create `OrderBuffer` as `GraphicsBuffer.Target.Structured` [S1, unofficial].
-3.  If false, create `OrderBuffer` as `GraphicsBuffer.Target.Append` [S1, unofficial].
-4.  If false, additionally allocate `OrderSizeBuffer` (`IndirectArguments`, size 1) and `BoundsBuffer` (`Structured`, size 6) [S1, unofficial].
-5.  Execute the platform-specific CPU sorting algorithm to generate the sorted order [S2, unofficial].
-6.  Upload the sorted order data to the `OrderBuffer` or texture buffers [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-7.  Bind the buffer to the GPU shader for reading and execute draw calls [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+**Parameters:**
+*   `CpuFallbackEnabled` (Boolean): Determines the active path. When true, the system uses the CPU fallback path [S1, unofficial].
 
