-### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Performance Bottleneck**: On mid-range mobile devices, the CPU sort and subsequent data upload can dominate performance [S2, unofficial]. At 233k splats, a single re-sort transfers approximately 5.6 MB of data, which is significant for fill rate and overdraw [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Capacity Limits**: CPU sorting is generally acceptable up to 300,000–500,000 splats [S2, unofficial]. Beyond this, LOD or pruning is required to maintain performance [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Platform Constraints**: On Android with Filament, the lack of compute shader support in the Java API necessitates this CPU-based approach [S2, unofficial].
